&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR COMMITMENT TO A STRONG AND INCLUSIVE TEAM:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re forging a future where everyone finds their rightful place and where every voice matters. Where uniqueness isn’t just accepted but embraced. That’s why we are committed to fostering the growth and development of every person, cultivating a sense of community through our Employee Resource Groups and advocating for inclusive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everpure is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, sexual stereotypes, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or any other characteristic legally protected by the laws of the jurisdiction in which you are being considered for hire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join us and bring your best.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring your bold.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pure and simple.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h1&gt;Senior Account Manager – Medical Affairs&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; London /Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you an experienced Medical Communications professional looking to take the lead on high-impact Medical Affairs programmes for a growing Women&#39;s health account?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Account Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team, supporting an exciting and evolving therapy area where innovation, strategic thinking, and scientific excellence come together. This is an opportunity to partner closely with clients, leading the delivery of impactful medical affairs initiatives that help shape scientific exchange and improve patient outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With opportunities to partner with clients onsite, this is an exciting role offering both variety and visibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Account Manager, you&#39;ll help drive the delivery of complex medical affairs programmes while building, collaborative client relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the delivery of strategic medical affairs programmes from planning through execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a trusted client partner, provide proactive advice, and ensure exceptional service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a variety of medical affairs deliverables including advisory boards, steering committee meetings, congress activities and symposia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the development of scientific slide decks, strategic communication platforms, digital medical education projects, and other medical affairs deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate teams including scientific, editorial, creative and digital colleagues to deliver high-quality work on time and within budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage project timelines, budgets, forecasts and financial performance across multiple workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify risks early and implementing practical solutions to keep programmes on track&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership and mentor to more junior team members, supporting their growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to account growth by identifying opportunities to expand programmes and strengthen client partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support process improvements and share best practice across the wider team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll bring experience managing complex medical affairs programmes within a medical communications agency and be confident leading client relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in a Medical Communications agency, in a Senior Account Manager or experienced Account Manager role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering Medical Affairs programmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing medical affais deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent project and financial management skills, with experience managing budgets and forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding organisational skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and stakeholder management skills with confidence working directly with global pharmaceutical clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring and developing junior team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, collaborative approach with a passion for delivering exceptional client service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to work on a high-profile account within an exciting and rapidly evolving therapy area, partnering with clients who value collaboration and strategic thinking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll enjoy:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working on innovative and strategically important Medical Affairs programmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to attend international congresses, client meetings and onsite workshops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative and supportive team culture where your ideas are valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to a broad range of medical affairs deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine opportunities for career progression within a growing account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible hybrid and remote working options across the UK&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing learning and professional development within one of the world&#39;s leading medical communications organisations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re looking for a role where you can make a real impact while continuing to grow your career, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a great compensation and benefits package including private medical insurance and a company pension, we are happy to talk dynamic working. We are also known for our friendly and informal working environment with Friday socials across our offices, regular wellbeing weeks, and Town Hall events. We offer excellent opportunities for career and personal development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to promoting a culture of diversity, inclusion and belonging. We believe that strength in diversity and inclusivity is a driver of our success.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.imgur.com/UuLTAa2.png&quot; alt=&quot;disability confident committed&quot; width=&quot;311&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Account Directors produce high quality advisory documents demonstrating a deep understanding of clients and issues. You will be regularly providing advice and analysis to clients, and developing an advisory voice informed by research, experience and awareness of market trends and events. You will manage some key workstreams as well as guiding executives and assistants on the account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Director, you will also begin to develop a network and build relationships with clients, media, advisers, Brunswick colleagues and other stakeholders. You will work to develop your media-handling skills and have a good understanding of Brunswick’s different sectors and specialist offers and how to connect them with clients as part of our one firm offering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive execution on client accounts within the Financial Practice team, managing workflow and key elements e.g. including press releases, investor presentations, shareholder, employee and customer communications, Q&amp;amp;As and other materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise our listed clients across a range of issues and communications disciplines, with the support of Directors/Partners, and drawing on independent experience and insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand complex sector issues e.g. M&amp;amp;A, IPO, shareholder activism, crisis communications and the attitude of media, the financial community, politicians/regulators, NGOs and other stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage complex media and financial stakeholder interactions, using advanced knowledge of media and other stakeholder landscapes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a key role in team management and dynamics, including supporting smooth team transitions, and serving as a day-to-day mentor to junior team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play an active role in drafting new business proposals and letters of engagement, including participating in pitch meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a network of analyst, advisors, journalist and media stakeholder contacts and relationships, proactively building a network to identify new business prospects and media contacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Together with Partners and Directors, proactively drive the strategic growth of Brunswick’s Financial Practice offer to clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 – 6 years of relevant experience either working in an advisory role within financial practice, or consulting experience advising clients with a financial focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of the interplay between corporates, the financial community, the regulatory arena and social stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of the disclosure obligations of listed companies, as well as M&amp;amp;A and IPO processes and workstreams, a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong sense of corporate positioning, and how to develop strategies that can translate into programs with real sustained impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the financial media landscape, with experience in media-handling, major announcements, earnings calls and capital markets days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in an entrepreneurial, fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong verbal and written communicator with high EQ levels and an engaging presentation style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A global perspective and able to thrive in an international businesses or organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credible and compelling with senior business leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A balance of creative and analytical thinking, bringing rigor, accuracy, and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven project and/or program management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural team-worker who prefers to work in a collegiate way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether you are joining a client facing team, a core services team, or starting out on your professional career journey, joining Brunswick unlocks a range of&amp;nbsp; employee benefits to support your financial future, health and wellness, family and community and continuous professional development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;About Brunswick&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brunswick is a global advisory firm. We help companies tackle high-stakes issues, navigate complex stakeholder relationships, and deliver high-impact outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our clients value our ability to anticipate, shape, and respond to the key players and forces in the financial and investment arena, regulatory and geopolitical universe, NGO community, workforce and beyond. They rely on us for deep experience, fresh perspectives and original thinking. So, in Brunswick you will find an exceptional range of experience and talent with a rich mix of backgrounds. From the beginning, we have prioritized attracting, developing, and retaining the best professionals in the industry, united by a culture of inclusivity, excellence, and intellectual curiosity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 1987 in London, the firm has organically grown to 27 offices in 18 countries across the Americas, Europe, Middle East, Africa, Asia and Australia. We operate as a “one-firm firm” with no individual profit centers. This allows us to assemble fully integrated, bespoke teams for each client, able to draw on the full resources of Brunswick anywhere in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
